   "text": {
    "L1": "A figure has rotational symmetry when it looks exactly the same after a turn smaller than one full turn.",
    "L2": "Do not count only the 360° turn. That turn makes every figure match, so it does not show rotational symmetry.",
    "L3": "The smallest matching turn is called the angle of rotational symmetry.",
    "L4": "The order tells us how many times the figure matches during one full turn.",
    "L5": "For a regular hexagon, each corner moves into the next corner's place after 360° divided by 6.",
    "L6": "So the smallest turn is 60°. The angle of rotational symmetry is 60°.",
    "L7": "It matches six times in one full turn, so its order is 6.",
    "L8": "Now use the same idea: order equals 360° divided by the angle."
   },
